course: dictionary
lesson: 14125
title: Milestone: a road stone or a big step
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. A milestone can be a real stone by a road. «The old milestone showed that the town was five miles away.» The sentence is about a road and miles, so the milestone is the stone.
explain: The other meaning is about life or a project. «Her first word was a big milestone for her family.» A first word is not a stone, so milestone here means an important event or step. Ask: what word would fit here? If "important step" makes sense in the sentence, you have the right meaning.
explain: People often reach a milestone, mark a milestone or call something an important milestone. Starting school and a team's 1000th goal are both milestones, because they are moments worth remembering.
fact: A milestone is a stone by the side of a road that shows how many miles it is to a town.
fact: A milestone is also an important event or step in someone's life or in a project.
fact: «Reach a milestone» means to get to an important point.
fact: Roman roads had milestones too, so the word has a long history.
fact: A good check is to swap in "important step" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The old milestone showed that the town was five miles away.» What is a milestone in this sentence? | A kind of cake | An important step in a project | A hard test at school | *A stone by the road showing the distance
exercise: «Her first word was a big milestone for her family.» What does milestone mean here? | A small dog | A stone by the road | *An important event | A stone wall around a garden
exercise: «Ben wants to mark the milestone when his team scores its 1000th goal.» What does milestone mean here? | A road that goes uphill | *An important moment worth remembering | A type of bridge | A tiny pebble on the pitch
test: «Reaching the age of ten was a milestone for Sam.» What does milestone mean here? | A road sign for drivers | A soft sofa cushion | *An important step in life | A wet, grey day
test: «Travellers on the old road counted each milestone to see how far they had come.» What is a milestone in this sentence? | A kind of bird | *A stone marking the distance | A soft sofa | A wide bridge over a river
exam: Sofia says, «Starting school was a milestone for me.» Which meaning fits best? | A hot summer day | *An important step in life | A short, rude reply | A stone by a road
